From d00d0e3b61029d3f9fcdfd2fb3cc59a7e0fce38d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:04:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] feat(libc): read guest va_lists portably in lifted
 builds

In a lifted build every VaList is a SysV va_list built by the guest or
by a bridge, so the libc formats and scans through FormatArguments and
its in-process scanner instead of the host's vprintf and vsscanf. The
libc's own variadic functions wrap the host va_list in a tagged VaList
through the shared APS5_VA_BEGIN macro, which the formatting and
scanning tests now use as well. Lifted builds keep the host C++
runtime and personality routine, store scanned long doubles in the
guest format, and round long double arguments from host callers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015taLuK6Ak1pT1P849L2eqq
